  "findings": [
    {
      "title": "Most customers who come back do it inside 45 days",
      "detail": "42.1% of customers with 180 days of history ordered again by day 90 and 44.9% by day 180. 80% of those second orders happened by day 45. Of the 344 customers still without a second order on day 45, only 14.0% ordered by day 180: this is where cohorts fall away, so the second-order nudge goes out on day 24, before day 45."
    },
    {
      "title": "Meta Ads brings one-time buyers",
      "detail": "22.3% of customers whose first order came from Meta Ads ordered again by day 90 (plus or minus 6.5 points), against 49.2% for everyone else (z = -6.03). Their first order averages $30.66 and their value by month 6 is $75.95 per customer. At the rest of the store's rate they would have brought 42 more repeat customers. 40.1% of them started with Rope toy bundle and Orthopedic pet bed, against 16.7% of everyone else, so look at what these ads offer before judging the channel on first-order ROAS."
    },
    {
      "title": "Refill products have a clock; set the reminders from it",
      "detail": "Dry dog food 12 kg: median 33 days, remind on day 29; Clumping cat litter 10 L: median 26 days, remind on day 22; Wet cat food 24-pack: median 20 days, remind on day 17; Flea and tick treatment, 3 doses: median 90 days, remind on day 83. Dental chews 30-pack: too irregular to time (p75 minus p25 is wider than the median); Rope toy bundle: too few repeats to time (under 30 intervals); Orthopedic pet bed: too few repeats to time (under 30 intervals)."
    },
    {
      "title": "Rope toy bundle and Orthopedic pet bed rarely start a repeat customer",
      "detail": "Rope toy bundle: 15.7% ordered again by day 90, against 47.3% for everyone else (z = -5.63); Orthopedic pet bed: 10.0% ordered again by day 90, against 47.0% for everyone else (z = -5.94). The best first product is Clumping cat litter 10 L at 58.7%. These buyers get the second-order nudge, pointed at a refill product. Flea and tick treatment, 3 doses is judged on day 180 because its median reorder interval is over 60 days: 56.4%, no clear difference."
    },
    {
      "title": "Newer cohorts come back more often",
      "detail": "Quarter pools 2026-04 to 2026-06 vs 2025-04 to 2025-06: 47.4% vs 34.1% ordered again by day 90 (z = 2.12), real change. Single monthly cohorts here are under 100 customers and swing by up to plus or minus 16.9 points, so compare quarter pools, not one month against the next."
    }
  ],
